From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:13:59 +0200
Subject: [parser] Validate expression errors before rewriting invalid LHS

When the operand of an assignment, prefix count operation, or postfix
count operation is not a valid reference expression,
`RewriteInvalidReferenceExpression` either reports an invalid LHS early
error or rewrites a call expression into a runtime `ReferenceError` (and
records a pattern error).

Previously, `ParseAssignmentExpressionCoverGrammarContinuation`,
`ParseUnaryOrPrefixExpression`, and `ParsePostfixContinuation` did not
call `expression_scope()->ValidateAsExpression()` before calling
`RewriteInvalidReferenceExpression`. As a result, inner expression
errors such as `{a = 42}` in `+{a = 42} = 1`, `++{a = 42}`,
`({a = 42}++)`, or `[{a = 42}.f() = 1] = []` were ignored in favor of
the outer invalid LHS / destructuring target error.

Validate the LHS as an expression before rewriting it as an invalid
reference.

